 "notes": "90% CL exclusion from Fig. 3 (top panel), recovered from the vector paths of chi_exclusion_publication.pdf in the arXiv e-print (fill_between boundary of the orange excluded region; axes calibrated against the figure's tick marks). Fixed-frequency SRF cavity at f0=1.294605478 GHz, i.e. mA'=5.354056807e-6 eV; the exclusion spans mass offsets ~-14.9 to +1.2 peV about that value (masses below the cavity frequency are probed through the upward tail of the SHM lineshape, QL>>QDM). Deepest point chi=1.50e-16 at zero offset (on the cavity resonance), matching the paper's quoted chi_90%=1.5e-16 at mA'=5.354 ueV. Scenario: randomly polarized dark photon DM, standard halo model, rho_DM=0.45 GeV/cm^3 (already the canonical density, no rescaling). Curve reported down to the figure's y-axis top (chi ~2e-15); masses differ only at the ~1e-12 eV level so many digits are retained.",
